course: dictionary
lesson: 14678
title: Preserved: kept safe and unchanged
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Preserve is a verb. It means to keep something safe, or to stop it from changing or going bad. Preserved is its past tense: «Gran preserved the plums in sugar so they would last all winter.» Here the plums were treated so they would not go bad.
explain: The same word can mean keeping a thing in its old state. «The council preserved the old mill for future children to visit.» Nobody has changed the mill, so it stays just as it was. Context tells you which meaning fits.
explain: Preserved can also be an adjective that describes something in good condition. «The fossil was so well preserved that we could see every bone.» Well preserved means it has survived in very good shape. To check a meaning, put it into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
fact: Preserve means to keep something safe, or to stop it from changing or going bad.
fact: «Preserved» can mean kept safe, kept in its old state, or treated so food lasts a long time.
fact: Food can be preserved by freezing, drying, salting, pickling, or with sugar. Jam is preserved fruit.
fact: «Well preserved» means in good condition, as in «a well-preserved fossil».
fact: Fossils and bodies preserved in ice or amber help scientists learn about the past.
exercise: «My gran preserved the plums in sugar so they would last all winter.» What does preserved mean here? | *Treated so they last a long time without going bad | Thrown away because they were old | Picked fresh from the tree | Eaten straight away
exercise: «The museum has an ancient fossil, well preserved for the future.» What does well preserved mean? | Very small and light | Painted bright red | *In good condition | Broken into small pieces
exercise: Which word means kept safe from harm or change? | *preserved | dropped | crumbled | wandered
test: «Dad preserved the lemons in salt and oil.» What is the best meaning of preserved here? | *Treated so they last longer | Squeezed for their juice | Bought from a shop | Grown in a garden
test: «The mammoth in the ice was so well preserved that scientists could study its fur.» What does preserved mean? | Moved to a new place | Painted in bright colours | *Kept in its old state | Broken into pieces
exam: «The old bridge has been preserved for the future, so people can still walk across it.» What does preserved mean? | Sold to a new owner | Covered in snow | Knocked down | *Kept safe and unchanged
